{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואכלת ושבעת", :translit "v'achalta v'savata", :gloss "and you shall eat and be satisfied"} {:he "ושכחת", :translit "u'sh'chachta", :gloss "and you forget"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacency: ושכחת follows ואכלת ושבעת in adjacent verses"}], :frame {:text "The Romans killed the inhabitants of Betar and left their bodies unburied for years until they were finally permitted burial; on that occasion they instituted the blessing HaTov veHaMeitiv. The Midrash reads the juxtaposition of 'you shall eat and be satisfied' (Deut 8:10) with 'and you forget' (Deut 8:11, culminating in 'and you forget YHWH your God') as teaching that the fifth blessing of Grace after Meals must mention the day of death.", :sources ["Berakhot 48b" "Eikhah Rabbah 2:4"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ואכלת", :translit "v'achalta", :gloss "and you shall eat"} {:he "ואכלת ושבעת וברכת", :translit "v'achalta v'savata u'veirachta", :gloss "and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless"} {:he "לה' הארץ ומלואה", :translit "laShem ha'aretz u'm'loah", :gloss "to YHWH the earth and its fullness"} {:he "והארץ נתן לבני אדם", :translit "v'ha'aretz natan livnei adam", :gloss "and the earth He gave to mankind"} {:he "אמרתי לה' אדני אתה טובתי בל עליך", :translit "amarti laShem Adonai ata", :gloss "I said to YHWH, my Master, You are my goodness — apart from You"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Derivation that blessings are required both before and after eating, from the sequence of the verse and the verses cited"}], :frame {:text "A person is forbidden to derive benefit from this world without a blessing, as derived from Psalms 24:1 ('To YHWH the earth and its fullness'). After one has blessed, the food belongs to him, as derived from Psalms 115:16 ('and the earth He gave to mankind'). The verse 'I said to YHWH, my Master, You are my goodness — apart from You' (Psalms 16:2) is expounded: once one has declared ownership to God, the goodness is no longer his own but permitted to him.", :sources ["Berakhot 35a" "Psalms 24:1" "Psalms 115:16" "Psalms 16:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ואכלת", :translit "v'achalta", :gloss "and you shall eat"} {:he "בכזית", :translit "b'k'zayit", :gloss "with a olive's-bulk"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ואכלת", :b "זהו בכזית"}], :frame {:text "The obligation to recite Grace after Meals applies only after eating a minimum volume of food; the olive-bulk (kezayit) is the minimum measure for many food-related commandments, as stated in tractate Berakhot.", :sources ["Berakhot 49b" "Yoma 80a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacency: ושכחת follows ואכלת ושבעת in adjacent verses", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Derivation that blessings are required both before and after eating, from the sequence of the verse and the verses cited", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ואכלת", :a-value 457, :b "זהו בכזית", :b-value 457, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:24.354644601Z", :model "glm-5.2"}